{"chunk_id": "892674c06962", "text": "Vasudeva recounts to Yudhishthira the origins of Parashurama (Rama of Bhrigu\u2019s line) and the destruction of the Kshatriya warrior class. Through a mistaken exchange of sanctified food prepared by the sage Richika, destinies are reversed: Satyavati bears Jamadagni, a tranquil Brahmana, while her lineage produces the fiery forces that lead to Parashurama\u2019s birth. Jamadagni\u2019s son Rama gains divine weapons from Shiva and eventually kills the thousand\u2011armed king Kartavirya Arjuna after the king\u2019s sons murder Jamadagni. Enraged, Rama repeatedly exterminates Kshatriyas across the earth. After giving the conquered world to the sage Kasyapa, surviving Kshatriya children hidden among common people are restored as rulers. The tale explains both Parashurama\u2019s legendary wrath and the later re\u2011emergence of Kshatriya lineages.\nVasudeva recounts Parashurama\u2019s lineage, the curse on Kartavirya Arjuna, Jamadagni\u2019s murder, and Rama\u2019s repeated extermination of Kshatriyas before their eventual restoration.\nThemes: Parashurama legend, curse and vengeance, Brahmana\u2013Kshatriya conflict, cosmic order and kingship, lineage and destiny", "vector": [0.0035527930594980717, -0.01989833079278469, -0.012658295221626759, 0.006638378836214542, 0.0008226547506637871, 0.019831106066703796, -0.014117058366537094, -0.003515819786116481, -0.03880174458026886, -0.020073112100362778, 0.013942276127636433, 0.0023125086445361376, 0.0046720742247998714, 0.0018889968050643802, -0.017948830500245094, 0.009014749899506569, 0.046142615377902985, -0.019105086103081703, 0.03398849815130234, -0.021605821326375008, 0.009781104512512684, -0.006137559190392494, 0.0015209449920803308, 0.011441539973020554, -0.004255284555256367, 0.02882568910717964, 0.004107391927391291, -0.019199199974536896, 0.009478596039116383, 0.002184782875701785, -0.014614516869187355, -0.0029460955411195755, -0.0021746992133557796, 0.006090502254664898, 